SUMMARY:Patient Zero: An Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:On display: October 3 – November 1\, 2026\nOpening Reception: Saturday\, October 3 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nMeet the artists\, explore the collection\, enjoy refreshments and live music\, and soak in the eerie atmosphere\, with scare actors from Factory of Fear: Outbreak haunted house adding to the experience. \nExhibit Summary\nIn conjunction with ARTfactory’s annual Factory of Fear event and fundraiser\, the Caton Merchant Gallery is proud to announce the opening of Patient Zero: An Exhibition\, a juried group exhibition featuring over 70 compelling works of art by 54 talented artists from across the DMV region. \nRunning from October 3 through November 1\, 2026\, Patient Zero blurs the line between fine art and immersive storytelling. Inspired by this year’s terrifying Factory of Fear theme\, Outbreak\, the exhibition transforms the gallery into a chilling archive of mysterious events\, unsettling discoveries\, and the unknown. \nThe exhibit embraces the eerie\, the haunting\, and the beautifully macabre. While artwork inspired directly by the zombie-themed haunted house is encouraged\, artists have also explored broader interpretations of darkness and mystery. Visitors can expect anatomical studies and scientific curiosities\, supernatural figures\, ghostly portraits\, dystopian visions\, folklore\, decay\, the ethereal\, and the undead. From psychological and gothic imagery to surreal and horror-inspired works\, the exhibition offers an unsettling variety of artistic perspectives. \nThe exhibition features a diverse range of mediums\, including photography\, sculpture\, painting\, digital art\, fiber art\, printmaking\, and more. \nRather than existing solely as a traditional gallery exhibition\, Patient Zero will become part of the immersive environment of ARTfactory’s annual Factory of Fear haunted house. During the haunted house run\, original works of art will be incorporated into the attraction\, allowing thousands of visitors to encounter the artists’ creations as part of the larger Outbreak experience. \nPatient Zero: An Exhibition opens with a free Artist Reception on Saturday\, October 3\, from 6–8 PM at the ARTfactory (9419 Battle St\, Manassas\, VA). \nThe exhibition will be open for regular public gallery viewing from October 3–10. During the Factory of Fear haunted house run from October 11–24\, the exhibition will be incorporated into the attraction and will not be available for standard gallery visitation. The exhibition will reopen for regular public viewing beginning Sunday\, October 25\, and remain on display through November 1. \nFeatured artists: Rockeats Alcoreza\, Mia Alvarenga\, Carter Austin\, Zee Berrios\, Andria Bielski\, Meghan Bogue\, Amanda Bohn\, Christopher Bradford\, Cher Carr\, AC Chen\, Margaret Connors\, Vicarrieous Creations\, Lauren Cunningham\, Katie Keller Dugan\, Heather Felt\, Amanda Fletchersmith\, Michele Frantz\, Mandi Fultz\, Whitney Fuss\, Denise Erin Gerhardt\, Shannon Gilbert\, Amber Goerner\, Elizabeth Hall\, Sara Humphries\, Amelia Irausquin\, Ginnefine Jalloh\, Jortt\, Rebekah Keener\, Jonathan Kincade\, Kirk Knoll\, Katie Kuntz\, Laura Lavarnway\, Maxwell Leitch\, Lenni Lemon\, Janet Hansen Martinet\, Moira Montgomery\, Tim Montgomery\, Meredith Moss\, Ketchup Jon Mustard\, Brad Nance\, Kym Nguyen\, Nancy M Patrick\, Jose (Pepe) Piedra\, Anna Polanco\, Jen Poteet\, Mandy Powell\, Sarah Richardson\, Maryann Segovia\, Xexilia Shadows\, Kelly Snyder\, Spades\, Richard Tyler\, Rebecca Visger\, Leah Watson \nFor additional information\, please visit the ARTfactory or contact the gallery for exhibition details. \nPress Inquiries\nJordan Exum\, Gallery Director\nARTfactory | Caton Merchant Gallery\n703.330.2787 | jexum@virginiaARTfactory.org\nhttps://virginiaartfactory.org/\nGallery hours: Tuesday-Saturday\, 10 am-5 pm\, Sunday\, 12-5 pm
URL:https://historicmanassas.org/event/patient-zero-an-exhibition/2026-10-07/
LOCATION:ARTfactory (9419 Battle St.\, Manassas\, VA 20110)\, 9419 Battle Street\, Manassas\, VA\, 20110\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://historicmanassas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/patient-zero-1080-x-1080-px.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="ARTfactory":MAILTO:jexum@VirginiaARTfactory.org
END:VEVENT
